# Dockerfile-specific ignore file (BuildKit): applies to builds using the Dockerfile next to it, so the
# whole repository can be used as build context without sending gigabytes of unrelated files.
# Strategy: ignore everything, then re-include only what the image needs (an "allowlist").
*

# application code and image dependencies
!p00_fundamentals/c02_fastapi
!p01_containerisation_and_cloud_deployment/c00_docker/requirements.txt

# never send generated artefacts, caches or secrets, even inside the re-included folders
**/outputs
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.env

# documentation, conda environments and tests are not needed at runtime
**/*.md
**/conda_env_*.yml
**/test_*.py
